Z||000005||william_thorniii||12-15-1999||04:16 PM||||Gentlemen,<P>I personally think that it depends what you are trying to achieve.  I prefer the looks of the 85 GT, 86 & 87 SE's for a muscular looking car.  When they are lowered with bulging wheels/tires and a DGP body kit you had better get out of their way.  There is something about those sharp angles and fender flares.  But I adore the looks of my 1987 SC with the DGP rear spoiler.  While the 86-88 GT's look good from the factory (except ride height).  So in conclusion, with mods, I prefer notchbacks... w/o mods I prefer fastback.<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||6
Z||000006||Reality||12-15-1999||04:22 PM||||Actually I like the lines of the '89. Yes I know it was never in production but it's still the best looking in my mind.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.public.iastate.edu/~jallen/fiero892.jpg"> ||||reg||1
